============================================================
2. AUTHENTICATION
============================================================

FlowFlix uses JWT authentication.

For protected APIs, frontend must send:

Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>

Example:

Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9...


Public APIs do NOT require JWT.


============================================================
3. PUBLIC APIs
============================================================

These APIs are configured as public in SecurityConfig.

------------------------------------------------------------
3.1 LOGIN
------------------------------------------------------------

Method:
POST

URL:
http://localhost:8081/api/login

Authentication:
NOT REQUIRED

Request Example:

{
    "username": "a",
    "password": "123"
}

Frontend JavaScript Example:

fetch("http://localhost:8081/api/login", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
        "Content-Type": "application/json"
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
        username: "a",
        password: "123"
    })
})
.then(response => response.json())
.then(data => {
    console.log(data);
});


IMPORTANT:

Save the JWT token returned by login.

Example:

localStorage.setItem("token", data.token);


